<title>UK: TransCo UK gas forecasts for February 13.</title>
<headline>TransCo UK gas forecasts for February 13.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransCo, the pipeline division of British Gas plc, has announced the following forecasts and data for gas use in the period February 11-13.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm == million cubic metres)</p>
<p>    Feb 11 (actual)   308 mcm, 72 percent of peak day demand.</p>
<p>Feb 12 (forecast) 291 mcm, 68 percent of peak day demand.</p>
<p>Feb 13 (forecast) 315 mcm, 74 percent of peak day demand.</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(seasonal norm 4.2 Celsius)</p>
<p>    Feb 11 (actual)   8.5 Celsius.</p>
<p>Feb 12 (forecast) 8.7 Celsius.</p>
<p>Feb 13 (forecast) 4.8 Celsius.</p>
<p>There is a &quot;high&quot; probability of interruption on Network Sensitive Loads in the East Midlands Local Distribution Zone (LDZ) on Thursday. The probability in all other LDZs is low. There were no interruptions on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
